# E021's Session A step blocks, in the E002 step language (runtime/iwp/spike/steps.py), run one
# step at a time through the session (Session.perform) by runtime/iwp/driver/clicks.py. A block
# starts at a "# --- block NAME" line and runs to the next one. Coordinates are the 800x600 stage's
# (walkthroughs/coordinates.md). The texts of new-game, quiet, dismiss, place-any and the three
# notices are E020's own (experiments/E020-wine-first-run/play.steps), unchanged: their coordinates
# are measured, and E020's rules (New Game from the title only, T41) hold here.
#
# The attack flow (e021_loop.py) is these blocks with two synthesised country clicks between them,
# each a plain `click X Y` at the country's proven point (experiments/E021-pro-session-a/points.py),
# sent through the same click-driver: attack-open, the target's click (the target panel is watched:
# it changes when the game takes the target), the attacker's click (then the loop polls captures for
# the gold quit-attack button: the battle is on), then exchange clicks, and leave-battle; or
# attack-cancel when the game did not take the target or the attacker. This is the order of the
# spike's attack_picked step (runtime/iwp/spike/cycle.py), which the E002 tour ran, with the
# attacker named by its own click instead of by the placement's pick.

# --- block new-game
# From the title screen only (T41): the order and the points are E002's loss-easy.steps (New Game,
# EASY, Play Game). The loop never sends this block from a board: New Game in the middle of a live
# game quits it, and with the human holding fewer than 10 countries the game credits a loss, writes
# its scoreboard file and shows the Scoreboard (F003; sitting 20261008T204817Z). EASY is a plain
# click: the setup screen of a later game may already show EASY. The computers' first turns follow
# (block quiet).
watch all
click! 100 585
settle
click 533 311
click! 565 532

# --- block quiet
# The computers' turns: the board unchanged for 4 s (a poll on the screen, bounded by the spike).
# F003: 15 to 33 s before the first human turn, 23 to 24 s after a pass. The loop repeats this
# block until the board is quiet or its attempts are spent.
watch 0 0 800 495
settle 4

# --- block place-any
# E020's own placement (its block `place`, unchanged): the first of the 44 proven country points
# that lights the placement row. The loop sends it only when its own choice of country could not be
# selected, so the turn is still played (the stack is then not the one the loop wanted to grow).
watch 265 530 270 26
click-until? 168 168 168 24 1000 55 193 49 261 42 330 105 441 142 385 153 433 188 399 235 441 239 282 178 283 132 238 139 166 277 177 358 60 344 110 307 160 390 163 393 98 473 139 440 190 509 223 566 143 525 89 593 86 682 99 760 129 685 153 746 196 668 211 748 264 655 282 750 411 698 436 639 446 515 404 521 343 454 363 448 444 372 453 377 410 308 425 333 305 412 294 321 262

# --- block place-commit
# ALL, then PLACE: every reinforcement goes on the one country the loop selected before this block
# (the placement row only lights for a country the human owns; the selection is the loop's
# synthesised `click-until?` on that country's point, with E020's own placement-row test). The
# ATTACK phase follows; PASS is block pass.
watch 262 502 276 70
click! 307 543
click! 497 543
settle

# --- block pass
# PASS, then CONTINUE when a card was awarded (E020's commit block, split: the Session A turn
# attacks between the placement and the pass). Sent once the attack phase is over and the turn is
# still the human's.
watch 262 502 276 70
click! 417 530
click-any? 402 531

# --- block attack-open
# The turn menu's attack button (the spike's ATTACK_BUTTON, 303,530), with the target panel watched
# (the spike's TARGET_PANEL, bottom left): the game asks for a target there. The loop then clicks the
# target and reads whether the panel changed again.
watch 10 502 250 70
click 303 530

# --- block attack-cancel
# The cancel button while a target or an attacker is asked for (the spike's CANCEL_BUTTON): sent
# when the game did not take the target, or no battle came up after the attacker's click.
watch 262 502 276 70
click 405 530

# --- block exchange
# One click of the battle's attack button (the tour's "ATTACK: one round", 337,531), with the
# battle result row watched (walkthroughs/coordinates.md). A plain click: a click the game does not
# answer is an observation here, not a failure. The loop then reads the board until the two
# countries' counts have changed and settled.
watch 545 502 250 70
click 337 531

# --- block leave-battle
# The tour's exit (tour.steps): the quit-attack button, or DONE on the move-in after a capture, each
# tried until the centre panel shows the turn menu's green. Candidate 1 is the quit-attack button,
# candidate 2 DONE; a failure is only noted (after a failed attack the turn has passed and neither
# is there).
watch 262 502 276 70
click-until? 0 192 64 16 600 456 531 495 540

# --- block dismiss
# A prompt between turns (a card or an event message) that keeps the placement row from showing:
# CONTINUE when it is there; the loop then waits for a quiet board and tries the placement again.
watch 262 502 276 70
click-any? 402 531

# --- block eliminated-keep-playing
# The elimination notice (runtime/iwp/driver/screens.py `eliminated`): of its two buttons in the
# bottom bar, the one that lets the computers play the game out, red, centre 665,531. The owner's
# decision (T38 round 4): keep playing. Sent once; the notice must go (the screen changes).
watch all
click! 665 531

# --- block game-over-continue
# The winner notice (runtime/iwp/driver/screens.py `game-over`): its one grey CONTINUE button in
# the middle of the bottom bar, centre 401,534. Sent once, after the loop has logged the game's
# end; the notice must go (the screen changes). What follows is read from the screen, never
# assumed: the next game starts only on the title.
watch all
click! 401 534

# --- block scoreboard-continue
# The Scoreboard (runtime/iwp/driver/screens.py `scoreboard`): shown after the game credits a
# loss, with one grey CONTINUE button in the bottom bar, centre 401,526. Sent once, after the
# loop has logged `loss-credited`; the screen must change. The next game starts only on the title.
watch all
click! 401 526
